WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.230
Yippee ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.490
Zootopia is finally coming out on Blu-ray
and DVD, so I wanted to take a look at some

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.680
of the characters who were deleted from the
final cut of the movie.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.740
I'm gonna breakdown who they were and how
they would have fit into the story.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.710
Just be aware that if you haven't seen the
movie yet, there will be a few spoilers, so

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.720
if that bothers you, check out my spoiler-free
review here.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.859
Honey Badger was a female friend of Nick's
who believed in the conspiracy theory that

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.240
sheep were secretly running the world.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.140
Honey lived in a bunker that was fitted out
with some hilarious anti-sheep weaponry ranging

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.559
from shearing scissors to a hedge trimmer
and from waxing strips to a golf bag filled

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:37.940
with fireworks.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.350
In real life, honey badgers are very fierce
animals and Honey's character was designed

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.859
to appear unstable.

00:00:43.859 --> 00:00:48.199
She had different sized eyes and went around
with stained clothes and food in her hair.

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:52.530
Some early concept art shows some of the funny
conspiracy theories that Honey believed about

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.530
sheep.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.249
And given that, in the end, we find out that
Bellwether's actually the villain, maybe Honey

00:00:57.249 --> 00:00:59.280
did have a point after all!

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.530
Honey's character wasn't completely lost to
the movie though as she turns up as Dr Madge

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.720
Honey Badger, the doctor doing research for
Mayor Lionheart on the imprisoned predators

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.620
at Cliffside Asylum.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.080
The Gerbil Jerks were a pair of annoying gerbils
from Little Rodentia who used to aggravate

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.170
Nick by deliberately running over his tail
in their little red car.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.270
And every time they did that, Nick would get
a shock from his tame collar which predators

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.060
had to wear in early drafts Zootopia.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.170
The tame collars were designed to keep predators
under control and I'll talk more about them

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.060
in my video on Zootopia's deleted scenes and
rejected concepts, which you can click right

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.810
here to watch.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:40.040
Koslov, the polar bear who carries Mr Big
into the room where Nick and Judy are waiting,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.670
has a 5-year-old son called Morris.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:47.240
Morris actually appears in a deleted scene
called "The Taming Party" which is a right-of-passage

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.270
ceremony in which young predators receive
tame collars.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:54.880
The scene features an emotional and tender
moment when Koslov gives his son Morris his

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.280
tame collar which signifies his son's acceptance
into Zootopian society.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.680
As he celebrates at the party, Morris gets
shocked by the collar.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:07.710
Actually, Cory Loftis, the movie's character
art director has said that Morris is the deleted

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.500
character he misses the most.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.170
Morris's look was deliberately designed to
make him appear innocent in comparison to

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.920
his gangster polar bear father Koslov.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.570
Doug the ram started life as a character called
Wooly who also worked for Bellwether, but

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.730
at her office rather than in their Breaking
Bad-style lab.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.660
Wooly was also a villain who managed to disguise
the fact that he was shredding paperwork by

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.770
looking like he was eating paper out of cans.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.380
Also using a corset and overcoat, Wooly would
disguise himself as a wolf, making him a clever

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.440
twist on the phrase 'a wolf in sheep's clothing'.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.100
By the way, at the end of the final version
of the movie, that phrase actually does come

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:50.340
to life when Bogo tells the wolf police officer
Wolford to put on a ram's mask to go undercover.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.330
The Razorbacks were an elite tactical police
team that would be deployed in the event of

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.880
predators getting out of control.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:00.870
They were named "Razorbacks" after the North
American term for a wild boar or hog.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.060
And just like wild boar, the Razorbacks had
the ability to sniff out predators and so

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:09.070
were sometimes also called "Sniffers".

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:14.170
During Zootopia's development, the team had
lots of different ideas for a goat character.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.410
Eventually, these culminated in a character
called Mabel The Old Goat who was created

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:20.400
as a meter maid partner for Judy.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.180
The scene that was storyboarded but didn't
make the cut was rather amusing and featured

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.960
Mabel telling Judy to keep up the good work
as in 50 years she could look forward to being

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.130
promoted to Mabel's position!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:35.620
Originally, Bellwether wasn't going to be
the movie's villain.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.930
Instead, directors Byron Howard and Rich Moore
planned to have a pig as the film's baddie.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.910
The reason for their initial choice was that
pigs are said to be very smart animals.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:48.040
This villainous pig was going to be called
Mayor Swinton and she was designed to be both

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.630
extremely clever and smartly dressed.

